{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>They have dealt corruptly with Him, not His children.</b> Meaning: when they corrupt their way, they bring evil upon themselves, and what evil do they bring — לֹא בָּנָיו, meaning they are not called children of the living El, as they of blessed memory said (Bava Batra 10a) — when Israel walk in the way of the Holy One, blessed be He, they are called sons, and when they do not walk, etc., they are called servants. And this is what the verse says, ״שִׁחֵת לוֹ״ — that they are not called the children of the Holy One, blessed be He. And the verse says ״מוּמָם״ — their blemish — because one might say: after all, the matter reaches the Father, the blemish of the children, heaven forbid. Therefore it says ״מוּמָם״, meaning the blemish comes from them, not from our Father, for He created man upright, as the prophet said (Isaiah 5:1–2): ״כֶּרֶם הָיָה״ etc., ״וַיְעַזְּקֵהוּ וַיְסַקְּלֵהוּ וַיִּטָּעֵהוּ שׂוֹרֵק״ etc., ״וַיְקַו לַעֲשׂוֹת עֲנָבִים״ etc. And this is what it says ״מוּמָם״ — meaning the blemish comes from them. And the meaning of מוּם, according to what they of blessed memory said (Sotah 3a): a person does not commit a transgression unless a spirit of folly enters him — which is an evil spirit, and it is called מוּם, in the secret of what the verse says (Deuteronomy 15:21) ״מוּם רָע״. And the drawing down of this evil portion comes only from the side of man's own deed." "<b>A generation crooked and perverse, etc.</b> For if they were merely crooked alone, the words of Torah would set the crooked straight. And what caused them to be corrupted? Their being עִקֵּשׁ וּפְתַלְתֹּל — meaning they strengthen themselves in their crookedness, as our eyes see in these generations, varieties of heresy through a crooked path; and when a person straightens out their crookedness, they strengthen themselves in even harsher crooked ways. And this is utter ruin of inborn nature."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:09.031914521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}